```json
{
  "pcr_probability": 0.12,
  "conclusion": "unlikely_pcr",
  "evidence": [
    {"feature": "HR", "value": 1, "direction": "against_pcr"},
    {"feature": "HER2", "value": 0, "direction": "against_pcr"},
    {"feature": "MammaPrint", "value": 1, "direction": "supports_pcr"},
    {"feature": "age", "value": 42, "direction": "neutral"}
  ],
  "report": "This patient has hormone receptor-positive (HR+), HER2-negative breast cancer with a high-risk MammaPrint result. HR+/HER2- tumors generally have lower pCR rates compared to HER2-positive or triple-negative subtypes, as they are typically less chemosensitive. While the high-risk genomic profile indicates a more aggressive tumor biology that may respond better to chemotherapy than low-risk HR+ disease, the overall probability of achieving a pathologic complete response remains modest. The patient's age is within the typical range and does not significantly alter this estimate."
}
```

